vite.config.ts<pre><code>import ts from "typescript";
import { defineConfig } from "vite";
import joltui from "joltui-vite-plugin";
import { vitePluginTypescriptTransform } from "vite-plugin-typescript-transform";

export default defineConfig({
    plugins: [
        joltui(),
        vitePluginTypescriptTransform({
            enforce: "pre",
            filter: { files: { include: /\.ts$/ } },
            tsconfig: {
                override: {
                    target: ts.ScriptTarget.ES2022,
                    experimentalDecorators: false,
                    useDefineForClassFields: true,
                },
            },
        }),
    ],
    build: { target: "es2022" },
});
</code></pre>

src/app/app.ts<pre><code>import {
    App,
    Lifecycle,
    lifecycle,
    type AppConfig,
    type ErrorHandlerClass,
} from "joltui";
import MainLayout from "./layouts/mainLayout.js";
import MyRouter from "./router.js";
import MyErrorHandler from "./errorHandler.js";
import type { User } from "./types.js";

export default class MyApp extends App&lt;MyApp&gt; {
    override readonly errorHandlers:
        readonly ErrorHandlerClass&lt;MyApp&gt;[] = [MyErrorHandler];

    constructor(config: AppConfig&lt;MyApp&gt;) {
        super(config);
    }

    protected override routerGenerator(): MyRouter {
        return new MyRouter({
            app: this,
            baseLayout: MainLayout,
            defaultTarget: "#page",
        });
    }

    get user(): User | null {
        return this.getData&lt;User | null&gt;("user");
    }

    @lifecycle(Lifecycle.BEFORE_INIT)
    async loadSession(): Promise&lt;void&gt; {
        const response = await fetch("/api/session");
        if (response.ok) {
            this.setData("user", await response.json());
        }
    }
}
</code></pre> <p>The generic parameter is the class itself: <code>App&lt;MyApp&gt;</code>. Every component declared as <code>CustomElement&lt;MyApp&gt;</code> and every <code>Router&lt;MyApp&gt;</code> or <code>ErrorHandler&lt;MyApp&gt;</code> then sees <code>this.app</code> as a <code>MyApp</code>, including your own additions such as the <code>user</code> getter above.</p>

Stage When it runs <code>BEFORE_INIT</code> After the DOM is patched and error handlers exist, before the router is created. Load session data, configuration or translations here. <code>EXTENSION_INIT</code> Immediately after <code>BEFORE_INIT</code>. Intended for setting up extensions and integrations. <code>AFTER_INIT</code> After the first route and all top-level components have initialized. <pre><code>@lifecycle(Lifecycle.AFTER_INIT)
reportStartup(): void {
    console.info(`${this.appName} ready at ${this.pathname}`);
}
</code></pre>

src/app/errorHandler.ts<pre><code>import {
    AuthenticationError,
    ErrorHandler,
    RouteNotFoundError,
    handles,
} from "joltui";
import type MyApp from "./app.js";
import NotFoundPage from "./errorPages/notFoundPage.js";
import { ValidationError } from "./errors.js";

export default class MyErrorHandler extends ErrorHandler&lt;MyApp&gt; {
    @handles(AuthenticationError)
    async signIn(error: AuthenticationError): Promise&lt;void&gt; {
        await this.app.router.redirect(`/login?target=${encodeURIComponent(error.path)}`);
    }

    @handles(RouteNotFoundError)
    async notFound(error: RouteNotFoundError): Promise&lt;void&gt; {
        await this.app.router.showErrorPage(NotFoundPage, {
            error,
            title: "Page not found",
        });
    }

    @handles(ValidationError)
    showValidation(error: ValidationError): void {
        this.app.setData("formErrors", error.fieldErrors);
    }
}
</code></pre> <p>Register the class on the application:</p> <pre><code>export default class MyApp extends App&lt;MyApp&gt; {
    override readonly errorHandlers:
        readonly ErrorHandlerClass&lt;MyApp&gt;[] = [MyErrorHandler];
}
</code></pre> <p>The App creates one instance of each class during <code>init()</code> and passes itself to the constructor, so handler methods can use <code>this.app</code>. A method may handle several types: <code>@handles(NetworkError, InternalServerError)</code>.</p>

src/app/router.ts<pre><code>import { Router } from "joltui";
import type MyApp from "./app.js";

export default class MyRouter extends Router&lt;MyApp&gt; {}
</code></pre> src/app/app.ts<pre><code>protected override routerGenerator(): MyRouter {
    return new MyRouter({
        app: this,
        baseLayout: MainLayout,
        defaultTarget: "#page",
    });
}
</code></pre> Option Meaning <code>app</code> The application instance. Required. <code>baseLayout</code> The default layout class (must use <code>@layout</code>). Required. <code>defaultTarget</code> Selector of the element inside the layout that receives the page. Required. <code>pages</code> Array of page classes. Optional when the Vite plugin supplies them. <code>baseUrl</code> Prefix for every page path; may contain parameters. <code>indexRoute</code> Path used when the location has no path at all (default <code>/</code>). <p>When the router is constructed it reads the metadata of every page and validates it: each page must use <code>@page</code>, each layout <code>@layout</code>, and each must be registered with its decorated class. It then builds a sorted route table. Invalid configuration therefore fails at startup rather than on the first visit to a page.</p>
